R-05 FEL options: register the fork's dovi-fel / dovi-fel-hwdec /
vo-frame_outputvo-dovi-p7-to-p81 in stock mpv 0.41.0 (patch 0007,
append-only series; verified to apply cleanly on a pristine tree
after 0001-0006).

Spec: ~/workspace/p115-player-re/full-restoration/R-05-fel.md S1/S2.
Stock mpv has none of these options, so every player-side set was
silently dropped (mpv_set_option_string failure, log-only).  This
patch only registers the options and stores their values; the
demux/decode/pairing machinery that consumes them in the fork is
the remaining R-05 work and is NOT claimed here.

Self-determined (NOT original values, memo S6.2): the fork's option
types/defaults were not extracted.  dovi-fel is bool default no;
dovi-fel-hwdec is a choice defaulting to auto (matching the
original's defaultOptions value per R-08); the vo sub-option is
bool default no.

diff --git a/options/options.c b/options/options.c
index 716c3e6..d85d6c6 100644
--- a/options/options.c
+++ b/options/options.c
@@ -808,6 +808,19 @@ static const m_option_t mp_opts[] = {
         {"vo", 1},
         {"decoder", 2},
         {"decoder+vo", 3})},
+    // R-05 FEL options (patch 0007, append-only series).  The fork
+    // registers dovi-fel / dovi-fel-hwdec (R-05 memo S2); stock mpv
+    // has neither, so the player's sets were silently dropped before
+    // this patch.  Types/defaults are OUR choice, labelled as such:
+    // the fork's option types and defaults were not extracted from
+    // the binary (memo S6.2).  dovi-fel defaults to no (the player
+    // writes it explicitly on every open); dovi-fel-hwdec defaults
+    // to auto to match the original's defaultOptions value (R-08).
+    {"dovi-fel", OPT_BOOL(dovi_fel)},
+    {"dovi-fel-hwdec", OPT_CHOICE(dovi_fel_hwdec,
+        {"auto", 0},
+        {"yes", 1},
+        {"no", 2})},
     {"video-latency-hacks", OPT_BOOL(video_latency_hacks)},
 
     {"untimed", OPT_BOOL(untimed)},
